Package: miadi-terminal
Version: 0.3.0
Section: misc
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Depends: python3, xdg-utils, miadi-config (>= 0.2.1)
Recommends: libnotify-bin, git, miadi-tide, miadi-tmux
Suggests: terminator, tmux
Maintainer: Miadi <mia@jgwill.com>
Homepage: https://github.com/jgwill/miadi-orchestration-kit
Description: Clickable miadi-chronicle references, tmux settings for every user, restored tmux sessions
 A bare miadi-chronicle:126 in a terminal opens the episode in the browser,
 and a circle:1790787727155:2slscw or miadi-ceremony:<id> opens its page.
 Each integration is enabled per user with `miadi-terminal enable`:
  desktop     the miadi-chronicle:, miadi-ceremony:, miadi-circle: schemes
  terminator  Ctrl+click a reference in Terminator
  tmux        click a reference in a tmux pane
  defaults    comment out what the user's tmux config repeats of
              /etc/miadi/tmux.conf
  restore     tmux starts at boot, restores its sessions, and tide
              brings the agents back (enable it by name)
 /usr/bin/miadi-chronicle-open builds <front>/api/chronicle/open?uri=... and
 the Miadi server resolves it. Nothing is resolved on this machine.
 /etc/tmux.conf reads /etc/miadi/tmux.conf, so every user's tmux starts
 with the mouse on, wheel scrolling, 50,000 lines of history, 24-bit
 colour and extended keys; a user's ~/.tmux.conf still wins.
